ng EBITDAR margin from **28% to 15.6%** and producing a **₹2.4bn net loss**. The tell is the ex-currency number: **a net loss of just ₹56mn**, versus ₹23bn profit a year ago — this is a *fuel* quarter, not an FX quarter, a reversal of FY26's diagnosis. Management's response is textbook: shrink capacity into the weak quarter (**Q2 flattish**), price harder (**Q2 PRASK >25%**), park old CEO aircraft, return damp leases, defer senior-management increments. The uncomfortable admission is that the yield lever is now uncapped and reactive — *\"we'll have to keep testing higher levels of yields also just to offset the increased cost\"* — with no target spread and no visibility, because the Middle East conflict, which management believed was closing at end-June, **has flared up again**. Every long-dated commitment (single-digit FY27 ASK, mid-teens FY28–30, 40% international by 2030, 300bn ASK by FY30) was nonetheless **explicitly reaffirmed**.","trig":[]},"lm":"","m":203015,"mem":0,"pdd":"","prev_stage":4,"prev_zone_vpe":null,"r":null,"s":"INDIGO","sig":"","sx":{"SMA_50":"5236.4","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_below_52w_high":"15.0","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","vpe_df_60d_sum":"1.6","vpe_zone_cumul_df":"0.5"},"t":""}},"s":"INDIGO"}